HST Office: the frame coat's shared base: frame and dialog-layout tokens, crisp corners in the shared
drawing helpers, one GTK CSS file per frame part and a switch per part.

- Design tokens (<vcl/hst/designtokens.hxx>; no existing value changes): the frame's surfaces, divider,
  menu surface/border/hover/shortcut and the selected-item indicator (= accent), light and dark, every divider
  and border at 3:1 or more against its surfaces (WCAG 1.4.11) and the shortcut text at 4.5:1; sizes
  FrameDivider 1, MenuItemHeight 28, StatusBarHeight 24, DocTabHeight 30; radii Menu 8, MenuItem 4; the
  dialogs' layout (layout::RowGap 6, MinGap 4, GroupGap 12, DialogMargin 12, LabelGap 6, IndentGroup 12,
  ButtonGap 4).
- The ribbon reads its colours from the tokens (Palette::aRibbon; hst::ribbon::Palette is that struct and
  paletteFor keeps its signature, its dark test and the HSTRibbon/OwnerDraw switch). The colours are the ones
  it had: nothing on screen changes.
- hst::design::DrawRoundRect (and so DrawCard, DrawPill, DrawFocusRing: the Start Center and the File tab)
  draws its border as one filled ring of whole pixels between two concentric outlines, the fill ending
  mid-ring, and moves every filled shape (the card shadow too) back by the half pixel Skia (curves) and GDI+
  add: no pale hairline arc or notch and no fill past the border on Windows. PixelOriginShift and
  FillPixelShape are shared; the coat's FillShape/FillAndStroke now call them instead of its own copy.
- The coat's push-button gap reads layout::ButtonGap (4 logical px, unchanged).
- GTK CSS: CreateGtkCss appends one fragment per frame part after the dialogs' CSS, each from its own file
  (vcl/source/hst/coat/css/{ribbon,backstage,sidebar,statusbar,menus,doctabs}.cxx, empty for now) and
  after a comment naming the part, so each part is styled independently.
- org.openoffice.Office.HSTAppearance/FrameCoat/{Ribbon,Backstage,Sidebar,StatusBar,Menus,DocumentTabs}
  (default true) and hst::coat::FrameCoatEnabled/FrameCoatActive (<vcl/hst/framecoat.hxx>): a part is on
  only with the coat itself on (UiCoat/Enabled, HST_UI_COAT) and never in high contrast.
- CppunitTest_vcl_hst_coat: the frame tokens' contrast and values, the ribbon palette from the tokens,
  the helper's corners at 100/125 %, light and dark, and its backend shifts, the CSS fragment order, the
  frame switches.

